insert into public.deep_prompts (id, position, files, title, plain_goal, why_needed, full_prompt)
select id, position, files, title, plain_goal, why_needed, full_prompt from jsonb_populate_recordset(null::public.deep_prompts, $j$[{"id":"Prompt 01","position":1,"files":"00.D1, 00.D2, 01.D, 02.D, 03.A–05.B","title":"Scenario Suite Audit, Deduplication & ~650 Atomic Test Expansion","plain_goal":"Clean up all 540 existing test scenarios and expand them into ~650 single-responsibility atomic tests.","why_needed":"In V18.1, S151–S180 in 00.D2 were verbatim duplicates of T01-S111–T01-S140 in 01.D, and several blocks compressed dozens of tests into prose paragraphs.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal QA Verification Architect and Formal Systems Specification Auditor. Perform a zero-trust line-by-line audit, deduplication, atomic splitting, and expansion across all 540 specified validation scenarios in the GeminiForge specification (00.D1, 00.D2, 01.D, 02.D) and author the missing atomic scenarios for Tracks 04 through 13 (03.A–03.B, 04.A–04.D, 05.A–05.C, 08.A).\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. Complete Deduplication & ID Remapping Table (S001–S190, T01-S01–S160, T02-S01–S190 -> Canonical GF-T<Track>-S<NNN> IDs).\n2. Full Atomic Scenario Matrices (~650 rows) in Given / When / Then / Falsification Gate (cargo test CLI command & metric) format, marked strictly as [SPECIFIED_TEST]."},{"id":"Prompt 02","position":2,"files":"00.A (§2.2–§2.3), 00.B, 01.B (§1, §3), 02.A (§2.1, §2.4), Track 12","title":"Cross-OS Kernel Sandboxing, Subtree Supervision & Temporal Policy Engine","plain_goal":"Write the production Rust blueprints for our 3-OS process reaper, AppArmor wrapper, and temporal policy engine.","why_needed":"Ensures every worker subprocess and forked grandchild dies in <15 ms on timeout and blocks two-step read-then-exfiltrate attacks.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal OS Kernel Security Engineer and Release Engineering Architect. Design the complete V20 implementation specification for crates/forge-sandbox, crates/forge-policy, and Track 12 native cross-OS installer packaging.\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. Exact Rust implementation of SubtreeSupervisor across Linux (prctl(PR_SET_CHILD_SUBREAPER, 1) + delegated cgroup v2 leaf cgroup.kill), Windows (JOB_OBJECT_LIMIT_KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE + AppContainer SIDs), and macOS (setpgid + lifeline socketpair EOF + kqueue EVFILT_PROC).\n2. Verbatim Debian (debian/postinst, debian/prerm, dh_apparmor) and RPM scripts for /usr/lib/geminiforge/gf-bwrap-helper.\n3. Clean-room Rust forge-policy temporal state-machine evaluator over authoritative_audit.db + SOCK_SEQPACKET credential proxy (mlock + zeroize)."},{"id":"Prompt 03","position":3,"files":"01.A, 01.B, 01.C, 01.D, 00.E (#1–#22)","title":"Track 01 11-Stage Clean-Room Pipeline, Static Unpackers & Locked DuckDB","plain_goal":"Specify the 100% non-executing binary/bundle inspection pipeline and hardened DuckDB forensic worker.","why_needed":"Replaces the Python AppImage script with a memory-safe Rust SquashFS + EROFS static parser and locks DuckDB external access before mounting untrusted SQLite DBs.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal Reverse-Engineering Systems Architect and Binary/Database Forensics Specialist. Produce the complete V20 implementation specification for the Track 01 11-Stage Clean-Room Inspection Pipeline (01.A–01.D).\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. Native Rust static parser in forge-worker (goblin + bounded backhand / unsquashfs -no-xattrs -o) enforcing chmod a-x, computing max(e_shoff + e_shnum * e_shentsize, max(p_offset + p_filesz)), and scanning forward for both SquashFS (hsqs) and EROFS (0xE0F5E1E2 at +1024) magic bytes.\n2. JSON schema and SHA-256 verifier for toolpacks.lock.json across Tier 1 (0 MB), Pack 09 (~70 MB), and Pack 10 (~620 MB) with --ignore-scripts=true.\n3. Expanded gf-electron-security.yml (ast-grep v0.45.3 selector: pair) matching true/false and !0/!1 across both /work/asar-src and /work/wakaru-out.\n4. Hardened forge-duckdb-worker over VACUUM INTO snapshots with SET enable_external_access = false; SET lock_configuration = true;."},{"id":"Prompt 04","position":4,"files":"02.A, 02.B, 02.D, 02.E","title":"5-Protocol Interoperability Spine (MCP, ACP v3.2.0, A2A, AG-UI 1.0, A2UI v0.9)","plain_goal":"Specify the Rust protocol router uniting MCP, ACP v3.2.0, A2A v0.14.1, AG-UI 1.0, and A2UI v0.9 in <500 baseline tokens.","why_needed":"Patches 5 upstream rmcp v3.5.1 bugs, upgrades ACP to v3.2.0 Conductor proxy chains, and enforces the Asymmetric 3-Class Dual Barrier.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal Distributed Protocols & Agent Interoperability Architect. Design the complete Rust implementation blueprint for crates/forge-protocols.\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. rmcp v3.5.1 wrapper implementing BoundedJsonRpcLineReader (16 MiB cap fixing rmcp#1030), dual result+error rejection (#1283), ClientLifecycleMode::Auto (SEP-2567 server/discover), and McpMux lazy spawning + 300s idle SIGTERM termination.\n2. agent-client-protocol v3.2.0 Conductor (_meta.proxy: ForgePolicyProxy -> ForgeFileLeaseProxy -> ForgeMcpBridgeProxy) + per-harness launch manifest table + 5-session Standby Process Recycling (copilot-cli#4113).\n3. AG-UI 1.0 + A2UI v0.9 React 19 allowlist + a2a-rust >= 0.14.1 (11 A2ABreak defenses) + 4-Meta-Tool Capability Gateway (<500 baseline tokens)."},{"id":"Prompt 05","position":5,"files":"02.C, 03.A, 03.B, 00.D1 (S001–S010)","title":"Orthogonal Computer-Use Engine, Accessibility Workers & CLI-Anything Mech 0","plain_goal":"Design the sub-50ms desktop and browser automation router across Linux X11/Wayland, Windows, and macOS.","why_needed":"Fixes trycua/cua#4894 (Qt6 D-Bus hangs), #4963 (GNOME Orca trigger), and #4906 (1.2s Windows root walks) while removing XIAddMaster on :0.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal Desktop Compositor, Accessibility, and Computer-Use Agent Architect. Design the complete V20 implementation specification for crates/forge-cu and forge-a11y-worker.\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. ForgeAccessibilityProvider inside forge-a11y-worker (250 ms cgroup.kill/TerminateJobObject watchdog): stateless/drained zbus AT-SPI2 (fixing cua#4894), CHROME_ACCESSIBILITY=1 with ScreenReaderEnabled=false (fixing cua#4963), and EnumWindows + ElementFromHandle(hwnd) (<2 ms, fixing cua#4906).\n2. Hardware-Tiered Environment B Virtual Display Pool (Xvfb/Weston on Tier E/C; Xpra + Xephyr -glamor on Ryzen 3500U Vega 8 Tier B; Mint 22 Wayland auto-route).\n3. Permanent removal of XIAddMaster on :0 (CONFIRM-01), forge-intent-guard (VPI-Bench defense), <1 ms TOCTOU Sobel check, and HKUDS/CLI-Anything Mech 0 JSON harness adapter."},{"id":"Prompt 06","position":6,"files":"04.A, 04.B, 04.C, 04.D, 00.A (§2.6), 00.E (#65)","title":"Tracks 05–07 QuickJS-WASM Mods SDK, AgentShield Scanner & llmfit Governor","plain_goal":"Specify the <4 MB Wasmtime QuickJS Mod runtime, AgentShield pre-trust scanner, and split VRAM/RAM MoE governor.","why_needed":"Resolves the 04.A TypeScript-in-Wasmtime contradiction and eliminates false-positive fatigue on example MCP configs using runtimeConfidence weights.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal Extension Runtime Architect, Static Security Analyzer, and Hardware Resource Governor Specialist. Design the complete V20 specification for crates/forge-mods, crates/forge-hw, the agentshield Pre-Trust Scanner, and the 25-Pack Store.\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. @geminiforge/mod-sdk TypeScript definitions, <15 ms swc compiler, static tree-sitter-typescript L0–L3 '$' capability scanner, and <4 MB wasmtime rquickjs guest emitting declarative A2UI v0.9 JSON snapshots (CONFIRM-05).\n2. Port of affaan-m/agentshield (268 rules) with runtimeConfidence source weighting (1.0x active-runtime vs 0.25x template-example capped at 10 pts/file).\n3. Vendored llmfit-core (v1.1.10) patches for split GPU VRAM + Host DDR5 RAM partial MoE offload (-ngl / --n-cpu-moe) and Windows 11 ARM64 IDXCoreAdapterFactory + QNN NPU probing."},{"id":"Prompt 07","position":7,"files":"00.A (§2.1), 00.D1 (S071–S090), 02.E, 05.A","title":"Tracks 08–09 Terminal Multiplexer (OSC 7501 + gf-tmux-shim), Shadow LSP & jj-lib VCS","plain_goal":"Specify the OSC 7501 terminal parser, tmux-to-pane shim, Shadow LSP, and Jujutsu multi-agent VCS.","why_needed":"Lets CLI builds and coding agents report progress and permission blocks deterministically into the Unified Approval Inbox without prompt scraping.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal IDE Workbench Architect, Terminal Emulation Specialist, and Version Control Systems Engineer. Design the complete V20 specification for Tracks 08 and 09.\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. OSC 7501 (revision 0.2) VT parser in crates/forge-pty (\\e]7501;state=...:kind=...:progress=...\\e\\\\), OSC 7501 ; ? ST capability responder, 256-record LRU cap per pane, superseding OSC 9;4, and <5 ms routing of blocked states to the Unified Approval Inbox.\n2. bins/gf-tmux-shim translating tmux split-window, new-window, send-keys, and capture-pane calls into native GeminiForge panes with FORGE_PANE_TOKEN capability grants.\n3. crates/forge-vcs (jj-lib v0.46.0 StackedTable op-log, algebraic conflict trees, <50 ms op undo) + Shadow LSP (Pack 05) + crates/forge-search."},{"id":"Prompt 08","position":8,"files":"00.A (§2.2, §2.5), 00.D1 (S091–S100), 02.E (§4 #10)","title":"Tracks 10–11 SQLite RRule Automation Engine, Zero-Token Pre-Wake Gate & Flight-Recorder","plain_goal":"Design the unattended RRule cron scheduler, scratchpad worktree runner, and W3C traceparent time-travel debugger.","why_needed":"Ensures background automations never burn idle LLM tokens (via the SQLite Pre-Wake Gate) and never mutate your main branch without 1-click Inbox approval.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal Background Automation, Durable Workflow, and Flight-Recorder Forensics Architect. Design the complete V20 specification for Tracks 10 and 11.\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. SQLite RRule scheduler (rrule crate) + notify filesystem/clipboard triggers + Zero-Token SQLite Pre-Wake Gate (checking has_actionable_work(agent_id) in <0.1 ms in Rust and suppressing LLM wakes when empty, fixing paperclip#3401).\n2. Strict Read/Scratchpad Mode (S092, S093) & Opt-In Ambient Mode (T02-S133) inside ephemeral jj workspaces (ambient/<job-id>).\n3. Post-Mortem Flight-Recorder & Time-Travel Debugger (S098) linking prompts, tool calls, memfd screenshot dHashes, jj op IDs, and temporal_policy_events via W3C traceparent."},{"id":"Prompt 09","position":9,"files":"05.A, 05.B, 00.D1 (S061–S070), 02.C (§3)","title":"Track 13 Multi-Agent Swarms, Typed Evidence Receipts & ForgeLab (Concordia GM + OASIS)","plain_goal":"Specify the 20-agent TaskConstellation coordinator and the grounded ForgeLab social/product simulator.","why_needed":"Prevents multi-agent hallucination cascades and sycophancy bias using Typed Evidence Receipts, Concordia Game Master checks, and Adversarial Skeptic personas.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal Multi-Agent Systems & Grounded Simulation Architect. Design the complete V20 specification for crates/forge-swarm (05.A and 05.B).\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. TaskConstellation DAG coordinator enforcing TLA+-verified Safe Assignment Locking (T02-S115/S116), Confidence Stepping (rejecting >=15% jumps to 100% without a new passing verification ToolCallId, T02-S122), and Typed Evidence Receipts (eliminating MiroFish#529 fabricated quotes).\n2. Clean-room Rust ForgeLab Engine (Pack 14): DeepMind Concordia Game Master (GM) Causal Referee, TinyTroupe Persona & Statistical Engine, OASIS 23-action social graph over authoritative_audit.db (<150 MB RAM), and Cross-Family Model Jury."},{"id":"Prompt 10","position":10,"files":"00.D1 (S015, S021–S030), 02.A (§2.3), 02.E (§3 #2, #9–#13)","title":"Quad-Auth PKCE Vault, 429 Pool Rotator, KV Cache Scheduler & Junie-Lite Two-Speed Router","plain_goal":"Design the credential vault, prompt-cache TTL tracker, and Two-Speed Frontier/Workhorse model router.","why_needed":"Routes routine mechanical worktree tasks to free/local Qwen 3.6/3.5 models while preserving frontier credits and KV cache prefixes.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal Identity, Cryptography, and LLM Inference Routing Architect. Design the complete V20 specification for Quad-Auth, KV Cache Scheduling, and Two-Speed Model Routing.\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. Quad-Auth & Keyring Vault Manager with Argon2id + ChaCha20-Poly1305 fallback vault when OS keyrings are locked (S015) or in CI (FORGE_USE_MOCK_KEYCHAIN=1).\n2. Junie-Lite-Inspired Two-Speed Model Router (CONFIRM-07): classifies Frontier Architectural Turns vs. Workhorse Mechanical Turns, routing Workhorse turns to local Qwen3.5/3.6 (Tier B+) or free/Lite tiers.\n3. KV Prompt-Cache TTL Scheduler (5-min/1-hr countdown badge), 15s Compaction Watchdog (fixing goose#5253), and union-merged model catalog (fixing jcode#1824)."},{"id":"Prompt 11","position":11,"files":"00.D1 (S018, S081), 02.D (T02-S120, S131, S142, S163–S164)","title":"Local AST-Biased Voice Co-Pilot (forge-voice) & Subprocess Diagram Canvas (mmdr)","plain_goal":"Specify the local push-to-talk voice pipeline and the 200 ms subprocess-isolated Mermaid SVG renderer.","why_needed":"Matches spoken words against your codebase's real Rust/TS identifiers and prevents malformed Mermaid diagrams (mmdr#112) from hanging the daemon.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal Audio/Speech Signal Processing Engineer and Vector Graphics Layout Architect. Design the complete V20 specification for forge-voice (Pack 17) and the Hybrid Diagram Canvas (Pack 08).\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. forge-voice pipeline: PipeWire/PulseAudio/WASAPI/CoreAudio capture with WebRTC AEC, automatic null-sink isolation for Environment B PiP virtual displays (T02-S120), Moonshine-Tiny INT8 / whisper.cpp Q5_1 coupled to a Tree-sitter AST Vocabulary Rescorer, and zero idle WH_MOUSE_LL hooks.\n2. Hybrid Diagram Renderer (Pack 08): executes mmdr v0.3.1 selectable SVG generation inside forge-worker --role mmdr with a 200 ms cgroup.kill/TerminateJobObject watchdog, falling back to client-side mermaid.js on syntax errors or timeouts (mmdr#112)."},{"id":"Prompt 12","position":12,"files":"01.A–01.D (T01-S134–S136, S153), 04.D (Packs 11, 12, 22)","title":"Dynamic Instrumentation (Pack 11), Mobile/Firmware RE (Pack 12) & Mobile Remote (Pack 22)","plain_goal":"Specify the isolated network-tap DBI sandbox, mobile APK/Hermes/Flutter unpacker, and Noise XX mobile remote.","why_needed":"Lets analysts inspect mobile apps and sign Ring-0 Sanction Gate approvals from their phone with zero plaintext relay exposure.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal Dynamic Binary Instrumentation (DBI), Mobile/Firmware Security Analyst, and End-to-End Encrypted Networking Architect. Design the complete V20 specification for Packs 11, 12, and 22.\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. Pack 11: isolated Linux network namespace (gf-bwrap-helper --unshare-all) wired via veth/usermode stack to mitmproxy + pbtk-from-binary v1.1.3 (isolated GPL-3.0 CLI) + Frida-MCP.\n2. Pack 12: static extraction of Android .apk/.aab (jadx), React Native Hermes .hbc (hermes-dec v0.1.7 isolated AGPL-3.0 CLI, Hermes v59–v99), and Flutter libapp.so (blutter).\n3. Pack 22: QR-code X25519 + Ed25519 Noise XX handshake (snow Rust crate) for receiving OSC 7501 / AG-UI / Paperclip Board approval cards on mobile and signing Ed25519 approval tokens."},{"id":"Prompt 13","position":13,"files":"NEW V20 FILE: 05.C — Organizational Agent Hierarchy, Atomic Checkout & Guidelines Engine","title":"Paperclip Org-Swarm, Atomic 409 Checkout, Zero-Token Pre-Wake & Junie Guidelines (05.C)","plain_goal":"Author new specification file 05.C uniting Paperclip's organizational swarm contracts with JetBrains Junie's guidelines hierarchy.","why_needed":"Gives multi-agent teams structured roles, budgets, atomic HTTP 409 task locks, Goal-Ancestry why breadcrumbs, and deduplicated .forge/AGENTS.md rules.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal Organizational Multi-Agent Architect and IDE Context Engineer. Author the complete V20 specification for new file 05.C (Organizational Agent Hierarchy, Atomic Checkout, Goal Ancestry & Guidelines Engine).\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. Clean-room Rust implementation of Paperclip's 9-Step Heartbeat & Atomic Checkout Contract inside crates/forge-swarm and crates/forge-db: (a) Zero-Token SQLite Pre-Wake Gate (has_actionable_work(agent_id) checked in <0.1 ms in Rust, fixing paperclip#3401), (b) Atomic Checkout (X-Forge-Run-Id returning 409 Conflict with zero retry loops), (c) Goal-Ancestry Breadcrumb injection, (d) Revision-Bound Plan Confirmations, and (e) Per-Agent Budget Auto-Pause at 100% spend.\n2. Unified Agent Identity & Guidelines Loader in crates/forge-search (.forge/AGENTS.md, .junie/AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, GEMINI.md) with blake3 deduplication and compilation of '# Explicit prohibitions' into forge-policy guards."},{"id":"Prompt 14","position":14,"files":"NEW V20 FILE: 08.A — Claude-Desktop-Class Workbench Design System & Iced Native HUD","title":"Claude-Desktop-Class React 19 Workbench, Pure Framer Motion Choreography & Iced HUD (08.A)","plain_goal":"Author new specification file 08.A defining the warm literary salon UI, Artifact split-pane choreography, and <2 ms Iced HUD.","why_needed":"Codifies the exact Parchment/Ivory/Terracotta tokens, Fraunces/Inter/JetBrains Mono typography scale, and scoped iced.rs Super+Escape overlay.","full_prompt":"ROLE & OBJECTIVE:\nAct as Principal Design Systems Architect, Frontend Performance Engineer (TypeScript, React 19, Vite, CSS Modules, Framer Motion), and Rust GUI Systems Engineer (iced.rs / wgpu / tiny-skia). Author the complete V20 specification for new file 08.A.\n\nDELIVERABLES REQUIRED:\n1. Complete CSS Custom Property token system (variables.module.css) for Warm Editorial Parchment (#F5F4ED), Ivory (#FAF9F5), and Near Black (#141413) themes, Terracotta Brand (#C96442) accents, Fraunces/Inter/JetBrains Mono typography, and Streamer Privacy Mode (S090).\n2. Pure Framer Motion (stiffness: 350, damping: 32) spring choreography for the Side-by-Side CodeMirror 6 + Shiki + A2UI v0.9 Artifact Drawer (eliminating legacy GSAP runtime) and Ring-0 Sanction Gate Modal (DOM event.isTrusted == true).\n3. Standalone native Rust bins/gf-emergency-hud built with iced.rs (wgpu primary with automatic renderer/src/fallback.rs fallback to tiny-skia CPU rendering, CONFIRM-08) mapping in <2 ms on Super+Escape."}]$j$::jsonb);
